# OneReason-0.8B Frontier SFT Epoch 2 -> GRPO LoRA - Epoch {{EPOCH}}

This repository contains one LoRA adapter checkpoint for the Kuaishou LLM4Rec
competition.

## Training

- Start adapter: official Frontier SFT Epoch 2
- Method: online GRPO with eight live legal-SID candidates per group
- Frontier GRPO data: 17,016 normalized recommendation groups x 2 epochs
- Prompt rule: `/think` and `/no_think` are normalized to `/no_think`
- Reward target: the final SID after `</think>`; the original thinking text is
  not used as a reward signal
- Forced-GT safeguard: probability 0.5 when a group has no live GT hit
- Advantage: group sample Z-score with standard-deviation correction 1
- Completed epoch: {{EPOCH}}
- LoRA rank / alpha / dropout: 32 / 32 / 0.0
- Target modules: `q_proj`, `k_proj`, `v_proj`, `o_proj`, `gate_proj`,
  `up_proj`, `down_proj`

## Files

- `adapter_model.safetensors`: LoRA weights
- `adapter_config.json`: the original checkpoint configuration, preserved
  byte-for-byte

The clean base model is not included in this repository. Load this adapter on
the competition-approved OneReason-0.8B base model.

## Evaluation status

Only a local Frontier-derived constrained beam-16 probe was used for
diagnostics. No official competition score or improvement claim is made here.
